      "writtenOn": "2022-12-27T09:49:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This name sounds a little bit off. As written, it sounds like if this is off it always removes the listener, and if it\u0027s on it only removes the listener for legacy apps. But that\u0027s not what this change does.\n\nWhat it does is, if off it removes the resolution listener upon resolution, if on it keeps it.\n\nSuggested wording :\n\n    /**\n     * When enabled, keep the resolution listener after initial resolution of a service.\n     *\n     * Before Android 14, resolving a service is a one-shot operation that removes\n     * the resolution listener.\n     * Starting with Android 14, the system will send updates to apps with {@link\n     * onServiceResolutionInfoUpdated} until {@link stopServiceResolution} is\n     * called.\n     *\n     * On Android 13- this change is disabled by default, removing the listener\n     * upon successful resolution.\n     * On Android 14+, this change is enabled by default, requiring apps to\n     * call {@link stopServiceResolution} to stop listening.\n     */\n\nSo that\u0027s for the wording, but see my other comment.",
